  "title": "Bonn intracranial EEG segments, sets C, D and E (Andrzejak et al. 2001)",
  "description": "This dataset is a lossless BIDS (iEEG-BIDS) repackaging of the intracranial sets C, D and E of the Bonn EEG database (Andrzejak et al., 2001). It contains 300 single-channel segments of 23.6 s each, recorded at 173.61 Hz from five epilepsy patients undergoing presurgical diagnosis. Sets C and D are seizure-free interictal recordings from the hippocampal formation and the epileptogenic zone, and set E contains ictal activity. The data support research on nonlinear time series analysis and seizure detection.",
  "methods_description": "Segments were cut from continuous multichannel intracranial EEG (depth and strip electrodes) after visual artifact inspection and a weak-stationarity check. Signals were recorded with a 128-channel amplifier using an average common reference, digitized at 12 bit and sampled at 173.61 Hz. The original ASCII integer samples were converted to BrainVision INT_16 without filtering, resampling, re-referencing or rescaling, and every sample was verified against the source text.",
